{"meta":{"method":"Directed degree-preserving edge-rewiring null with shuffled weights","null_model":"Each replicate starts from the directed philosopher graph and performs 10 directed double-edge swaps per original arc. NetworkX directed_edge_swap preserves every node's in-degree and out-degree, the node set, and directed arc count while rewiring endpoints. The observed multiset of aggregated edge weights is then shuffled over the rewired arcs. Thus the null preserves the global edge-weight distribution and total weight, but not node strengths or the association between particular weights and endpoints.","score":"For the observed graph and every null replicate, run NetworkX Louvain on the directed weighted graph with weight='weight', default resolution and threshold, and the same fixed seed 260927; calculate directed modularity for that run's partition.","seed":260927,"randomizations":100,"swaps_per_arc":10,"interpretation":"The empirical p-value is (1 + null scores at least as large as observed) / (B + 1). It tests the observed weighted modularity against this degree- and weight-distribution-preserving null; it does not identify philosophical schools or establish that a partition is objectively correct."},"stats":{"nodes":1444,"directed_arcs":11135,"total_weight":15758.0,"observed_modularity":0.5522195186263823,"observed_communities":78,"random_mean":0.2582568556872886,"random_sd":0.001819071602533161,"random_min":0.25088339160001905,"random_max":0.2622912766405437,"exceedances":0,"empirical_p":0.009900990099009901,"scores":[0.25730541121220746,0.25552128307705707,0.2588522556413566,0.2576714992842707,0.25942771926982094,0.25975910136305974,0.2554418394887221,0.2576942003289022,0.25460442988756793,0.2583487128850002,0.2610620213158339,0.2593932549199974,0.256564113573298,0.2585663521532309,0.25755380179794857,0.2613157519024941,0.26025526235343976,0.26120429649869426,0.25951402109463056,0.25825047861469774,0.2558353121808836,0.25936080817233104,0.25921153380274553